# Not this checkout's code. `.claude/worktrees/` holds git worktrees of OTHER
# branches, created by the delivery workflows, so `prettier --check .` reports
# another branch's formatting against paths under `.claude/`. Measured on #148:
# two planted files there fail `format:check` on a tree whose own sources are
# clean. CI is unaffected — a runner has no worktrees.
#
# ⚠️ REDUNDANT TODAY, and kept deliberately rather than by oversight (#155).
# Prettier 3 reads `.gitignore` as well as this file, and `.gitignore` already
# ignores `.claude/` — measured by deleting this line and planting an
# unformatted file under `.claude/worktrees/`, which `format:check` still does
# not report. It becomes load-bearing again the moment `.gitignore` stops
# covering the whole directory, which committing anything under `.claude/`
# (a skill, a settings file) would do. Insurance against a one-line change
# elsewhere, and that is a measured claim rather than an assumed one.
.claude/

